%S A171742 24,300,30222192,4838419019
%N A171742 First 4-fold intrinsically n-palindrome (given in base ten).
%C A171742 Given the size of the first 3-fold 6-palindrome (13 base-ten digits; see A171705 or A171741), a fifth term is going to be difficult.
%C A171742 a(6) = A171705(4) <= 40968^5 = 115404784440424844525568, a 6-digit palindrome in bases 10241, 13655, 20483, 40967. - _Jeff Sponaugle_, Oct 12 2026
%e A171742 a(2)=24 is 11 in base 23, 22 in base 11, 33 in base 7 and 44 in base 5.
%e A171742 a(3)=300 is 1A1 in base 13, 363 in base 9, 454 in base 8 and 606 in base 7.
%Y A171742 Cf. A171701, A171702, A171703, A171704, A171705, A171706, A171740, A171741.
